Does `bestmove 0000` need a DRAWN root, or is it general to an empty restriction?

| root | restriction | info lines | nodes | bestmove | info strings |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
  (threefold fixture validates: True)
| threefold (DRAWN) | e2e4 (illegal) | 10 | 0 | **0000** | ['info string searchmoves restriction has no legal root moves'] |
| bare FEN (NOT drawn) | e2e4 (illegal) | 10 | 0 | **0000** | ['info string searchmoves restriction has no legal root moves'] |

=> if the NON-drawn root also gives 0000, this is a general `searchmoves` hazard, not a drawn-root one.
